ess on  the Clone Wars and rebel leader writer  azandi on Star Wars Rebels another  veteran of the Clone Wars animated  series also pops up in episode 6 that  doomed New Republic trooper on the  prison ship is played by Matt Lanter the  voice of animated Anakin Skywalker  lanter has voiced the man who would be  Darth Vader in more than 100 television  episodes which means he's played the  part more than any other actor the  Mandalorian is full of nods to Star Wars  past whether their tributes to the  original trilogy the prequel trilogy or  Beyond in chapter 6 though the show also  makes time to pay tribute to the people  who made the Mandalorian itself when the  mercenary crew arrives on the prison  ship for the task at hand they walk past  the cell that contains a four-armed  monkey-like creature that belongs to the  ardenian race that species is a  relatively new addition to the Star Wars  Canon the alien first appeared in Solo a  Star Wars story in 2018 in the form of  agile pilot Rio Durant Rio was voiced by  John Favreau the Creator and executive  producer of the Mandalorian those X-Wing  fighters who make an explosive  appearance at the end of the episode are  named jib Dodger sash Kettler and  Trapper wolf they're betrayed by Rick  famuia Dever chow and Dave filoni all of  them directors of various episodes of  the Mandalorian the opening of the  mandalorians first season finale offers  a bit of much-needed comic relief to cut  the high-stakes tension set up by the  last episode it also offers a bit of a  callback to a joke from a previous  episode about a beloved part of Star  Wars lore remember in chapter 6 when the  mercenary Mayfield took offense at being  compared to a stormtrooper it's because  Stormtroopers are notoriously terrible  shots the two speedier bike riding Scout  Troopers shown in episode 8 of the  Mandalorian can't hit anything either  even when firing their blasters in a low  stakes no stress situation they're  firing a feast of debris just because  they're bored and they still can't hit a  thing  in the eighth and final episode of the  mandalorian's first season viewers  finally get an information dump of  background info on the mysterious and  compelling ex-rebel fighter Cara Dune  one major Little Nugget as revealed by  moff Gideon is that the former Rebel  Shock Trooper hails from the planet  Alderaan the home planet of Princess  Leia or at least it was the home of  Princess Leia until it was destroyed by  the Death Star back in Star Wars A New  Hope craving Justice for her people  would have been a pretty motivating  factor for Cara Dune who then decided to  become an active member of the Rebellion  because of her Rebel history Cara also  mentions her fear of getting  interrogated with a mind flare that's  more of a horror fantasy term like  something out of stranger things but in  the Star Wars Universe Cara is most  likely referring to something like the  bore gullet that's the purple-skinned  psychic creature that painfully  interrogated Bodhi rook in Rogue one  it's basically an alien lie detector  while also breaking someone's brain as  it works in a major moment of the  Mandalorian chapter mop Gideon cuts a  path to Freedom out of his downed TIE  fighter with the use of a lightsaber but  this is not just any lightsaber it's a  black lightsaber as it isn't cast in a  customary neon shade this is a very cool  looking Star Wars weapon and also an  instant indication that moff Gideon is  truly a dark force to be feared his dark  saber as well the darksaber the  ceremonial weapon traditionally bestowed  on the leader of Mandalore first forged  by an ancient Mandalorian Jedi it's  popped up throughout the Star Wars  animated Canon it was last seen on Star  Wars Rebels when Rebel fighter Sabine  Wren passed it along to death watch  leader bocatan to more effectively fight  the Empire the fact that mob Gideon now  has this coveted weapon is bad news all  around as he's an imperial die hard that  means good guy or perhaps a lot of good  guys had to die for Gideon to get his  hands on this all poses a lot of  questions which can only be answered by  another season of the Mandalorian check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more Looper videos about Star  Wars are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the Bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

